### 3. ERROR HANDLING

#### ❌ BEFORE (No Error Handler)
```javascript
// If an error occurs, server crashes
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(req.query.data); // Can crash
  res.json(data);
});
```

**Result:** Server crashes, no error response

#### ✅ AFTER (Comprehensive Error Handling)
```javascript
// Global error handler
app.use((error, req, res, next) => {
  const statusCode = error.statusCode || 500;
  const isDevelopment = NODE_ENV === 'development';

  console.error({
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    error: {
      message: error.message,
      stack: isDevelopment ? error.stack : undefined,
    },
  });

  res.status(statusCode).json({
    status: 'error',
    message: isDevelopment ? error.message : 'Internal server error',
    ...(isDevelopment && { stack: error.stack }),
  });
});

// 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => {
  res.status(404).json({
    status: 'error',
    message: 'Route not found',
  });
});

// Unhandled rejection handler
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Global error middleware
- ✅ 404 handler
- ✅ Graceful error responses
- ✅ Error logging
- ✅ Different dev/prod messages
- ✅ Unhandled rejection handler

---

### 4. REQUEST LOGGING

#### ❌ BEFORE (No Logging)
```javascript
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
  // No request logging at all
});
```

**Issues:**
- No audit trail
- Cannot debug issues
- Cannot detect attacks

#### ✅ AFTER (Structured Logging)
```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = Date.now();

  res.on('finish', () => {
    const duration = Date.now() - start;
    console.log({
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      method: req.method,
      path: req.path,
      statusCode: res.statusCode,
      duration: `${duration}ms`,
      ip: req.ip,
    });
  });

  next();
});
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Every request logged
- ✅ JSON structured format
- ✅ Response time tracked
- ✅ Status code recorded
- ✅ Client IP captured
- ✅ Audit trail available

---

### 5. SECURITY MIDDLEWARE

#### ❌ BEFORE (No Security Middleware)
```javascript
app.use(express.json());
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // No security measures
  res.json([...]);
});
```

**Missing:**
- No security headers
- No injection protection
- No rate limiting
- No body size limits
- No CORS handling

#### ✅ AFTER (Comprehensive Security)
```javascript
// Security headers
app.use(helmet());

// Body parser with limits
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ limit: '10kb', extended: true }));

// NoSQL injection prevention
app.use(mongoSanitize());

// Rate limiting
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 100,
  message: 'Too many requests from this IP',
});

app.use('/api/', limiter);

// CORS (optional)
const cors = require('cors');
app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(','),
  credentials: true,
}));
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Security headers (helmet)
- ✅ Body size limits (10KB)
- ✅ NoSQL injection prevention
- ✅ Rate limiting
- ✅ CORS protection
- ✅ Configurable origins

