# Before & After: Code Comparison

## 1. Error Handling

### ❌ BEFORE (Vulnerable)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
```

**Issues:**
- No try-catch blocks
- Unhandled errors crash the server
- No error responses

### ✅ AFTER (Secure)
```javascript
app.get('/api/users', (req, res) => {
  try {
    const { limit = 10, offset = 0 } = req.query;

    // Validation logic...

    const users = allUsers.slice(parsedOffset, parsedOffset + parsedLimit);

    res.json({
      data: sanitizedUsers,
      pagination: { limit: parsedLimit, offset: parsedOffset, total: allUsers.length },
    });
  } catch (error) {
    handleError(res, error, 'Failed to fetch users', 500);
  }
});

// Global error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Error:', err);
  handleError(res, err, 'Internal server error', 500);
});
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Try-catch blocks
- ✅ Centralized error handler
- ✅ Safe error messages
- ✅ Global error middleware

