# Quick Reference Card

## Security Issues at a Glance

### 🔴 Critical Issues (Fix First)

#### 1. No Input Validation
```
❌ /users?limit=abc        → Accepted (DANGEROUS)
❌ /users?limit=-999       → Accepted (DANGEROUS)
✅ /users?limit=abc        → Rejected with 400
✅ /users?limit=101        → Rejected with 400
```

#### 2. Missing Security Headers
```
❌ No X-Frame-Options      → Vulnerable to clickjacking
❌ No X-Content-Type       → Vulnerable to MIME sniffing
❌ No CSP                  → Vulnerable to XSS
✅ Helmet adds all headers automatically
```

#### 3. No Error Handling
```
❌ Error → Server crash + stack trace
❌ Client sees: Internal Server Error (500)
✅ Error → Caught + logged + safe response
✅ Client sees: { error: "Invalid limit" } (400)
```

#### 4. No Rate Limiting
```
❌ 1000s of requests/second → Resource exhaustion
✅ 100 requests/15 min → Protection from DoS
```

#### 5. No Body Size Limits
```
❌ 1GB JSON payload → Memory exhaustion
✅ 10KB limit → Rejected with 413 error
```

#### 6. Information Disclosure
```
❌ Stack traces visible to users
❌ Error details exposed
✅ Production mode hides sensitive info
✅ Errors logged internally only
```

#### 7. No Logging
```
❌ Can't track requests
❌ Can't detect attacks
❌ Can't debug issues
✅ All requests logged with timestamp, IP, duration
```

